## Delivered boundary

Native full cost/entry controls, hosted sparse journey and scoped offline publication under host-wide caps.

## Ownership and possible overlap

Host cost/publication integration and timed network fixtures; allocate exclusive measured runs.

Independent ready packages may proceed together only after file/service ownership is reserved. Use separate leaf modules or isolated checkouts; shared migrations, command schemas, source/selection types, renderer lifetimes, runtime scheduling and performance sessions have one owner at a time. If actual code inspection finds an unproved shared boundary, add a dependency or serialize that work before coding. No promised worker count follows from the graph.

## Ordered work

Follow this package's task order. Original identifiers remain traceable; a reference to another former stage means its needed published contract, not an implicit global sequence. All native interaction, backend/persistence, authority, correctness and applicable resource obligations remain included.

### Task 05.T11

- [ ] **05.T11.** Complete the H3/H4 native entry card and host resource controls on the same scale fixture: known/unknown published and additional-download sizes, peak disk/RAM/GPU, continuing traffic/activity owner, supported profiles and external sign-in status. Add default cheap checks, an optional bounded trusted benchmark, explicit ready/adjusted/partial/refused states and continuing device/host/participant admission. Include changed manifests, inaccurate sizes, data/decode peaks, cancellation and persisted download counters. Use the existing sparse loader and configured network/offline policy; no second visitor cache or automatic provider/code installation.

### Task 05.T12

- [ ] **05.T12.** Complete the B33–B36 hosted route: an identified remote editor and restricted public visitor share this same supplied street/house/ball/Sands with independent views/detail budgets; an accepted local customization arrives through a scoped delta/asset change. Reuse verified asset transport behind workspace-principal authorization and bounded control/asset/presence streams. Include a Sand using a separate Organ's public data and another requiring the visitor's own login; missing optional access stays localized. Exercise cap reached, slow reader, frame-origin changes, host disconnect/restart, cached viewing/local drafts, reconnect reconciliation, revoke and last-lease release. Record host and client results against the hosted starter subprofile; this proves hosting/navigation, not shared rigid-body science.

### Task 06.T07

- [ ] **06.T07.** Extend B33–B36/H3–H5 to selected-profile offline publication and hosted packed/chunk delivery. Verify access-compatible payload partitioning/projections, mandatory/optional closure, transfer/artifact hash binding, finite versus unknown external totals, actual/estimated accounting and persistent caps through 30-minute reconnect/slow-reader sessions. Expand participant load only against measured host-wide budgets and existing admission guards. A pack mixing denied data cannot be served whole to satisfy a partial view.

